  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a shared target relationship with 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets KP-4 through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a modulator of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which is a known inhibitor of KP-4. This implies that Mollicellin N may influence the activity of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, potentially altering its interaction with KP-4. The presence of multiple indirect pathways connecting Mollicellin N to KP-4 through 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid suggests a complex regulatory mechanism, possibly involving the enzyme's role in cellular processes that are modulated by Mollicellin N. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a central mediator in the relationship between Mollicellin N and KP-4.",
